This example service is configured with the following values:
<ul>
 	<li><strong>Name: </strong>It can be any name as long as it matches the name (ID) used in the code.</li>
 	<li><strong>Type:</strong> In this case, HTTP service is selected. This ensures the Service Framework behind the scenes uses the correct client (HTTP).</li>
 	<li><strong>Service Mode:&nbsp;</strong>To call the service endpoint, the value needs to be "Live."</li>
 	<li><strong>Log Name Prefix:&nbsp;</strong>If you want to debug and have all request and response data in a dedicated file for this service, fill this in.</li>
 	<li><strong>Communication Log Enabled:&nbsp;</strong>This must be enabled to debug the requests and responses through logging.</li>
 	<li><strong>Force PRD Behavior in Non-PRD Environments:&nbsp;</strong>If you filter the logs and want to test as if it is a production environment, enable this.</li>
